 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Exit Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an exit survey?\", \"a\": \"An exit survey is a short questionnaire a departing employee fills in about why they are leaving and what their time at the company was like. It goes out around the last day. Unlike a conversation with HR, the answers are written down, which lets them be counted across every departure.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an exit survey form?\", \"a\": \"Tell Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> who gets the survey, when it goes out, and which reasons for leaving you want to count. It builds the exit survey form and its response table, and it is free to start. Ask for one version for hourly staff and one for salaried roles if their questions differ.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good questions to ask in an exit survey?\", \"a\": \"Good exit survey questions are specific enough to count. Four examples follow. What is your main reason for leaving? What would have changed your decision? Did your manager support your growth? Would you work here again? Read the results beside your yearly <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement-survey'>employee engagement survey</a>, which hears from the people who stayed.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should I be honest in an exit survey?\", \"a\": \"Yes, with care. Stick to facts the company can act on, such as workload, pay against offers you received or a promotion that never came. Leave out personal attacks. Before you write anything you would not say to your manager, ask HR who reads the answers.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should you fill out an exit survey?\", \"a\": \"Usually, yes. It takes a few minutes, and specific answers can change things for the colleagues who stay. Check first whether it is confidential or anonymous. A confidential survey shows HR your name, while an anonymous one stores no identity at all.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free exit survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Survey vendors and university HR offices post free exit survey templates, and any of them makes a fair first draft. A template stops at the questions. Emergent turns those questions into a working survey with its own send rule and no cap on responses.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should an employee exit survey include?\", \"a\": \"About 10 to 15. Lead with the main reason for leaving, then a few ratings on pay and on the manager. One open box at the end catches anything the list missed. Borrow wording from your pulse survey where it fits, and exit answers will line up with what staff said while they were still there.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an exit interview form include?\", \"a\": \"An exit interview form needs the leaver's name, role, manager, and last day at the top. Below that go the main reason for leaving and three or four open prompts for the conversation, each with room for the interviewer's notes. End with a yes or no on rehire eligibility.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is exit survey software used for?\", \"a\": \"Exit survey software sends the survey when HR records a departure and reports reasons for leaving by team over time. Engagement suites usually charge per employee for it. An app built in Emergent has no per-seat pricing, and on paid plans its code can go to your GitHub.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an exit survey for students different?\", \"a\": \"Only in audience and questions. A student version goes to graduating seniors and asks about advising and courses, then whether they would recommend the program. Universities read the answers program by program to decide where the curriculum needs work.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
